        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Is NordicTrack better than ProForm?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              At the top of each range, yes — NordicTrack's flagships generally have heavier frames, larger screens and wider incline and decline ranges. In the middle of the market the two overlap, and a top ProForm can match or beat an entry NordicTrack at a similar price. Compare the two specific models rather than the brands.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Are NordicTrack and ProForm the same company?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Yes. Both are owned by iFIT Health &amp; Fitness, formerly ICON Health &amp; Fitness. They share engineering resources and, on touchscreen models, the same iFIT software. NordicTrack is positioned as the premium line and ProForm as the value line.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Do NordicTrack and ProForm use the same iFIT app?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Yes. Touchscreen models from both brands run iFIT, with the same classes and the same automatic speed and incline control. What differs is the hardware it runs on — screen size and incline range shape the experience more than the badge does. The subscription question applies equally to both.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Why is ProForm cheaper than NordicTrack?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Mostly lighter-duty hardware: frames and motors engineered for moderate household use rather than heavy, frequent running, plus generally smaller screens and narrower incline ranges. That is a deliberate positioning choice, not a sign of poor quality, and for walking and moderate running it is often a sensible trade.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Which is better for running, NordicTrack or ProForm?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For regular or heavier running, NordicTrack's upper tiers are generally the safer bet because of their stronger continuous-duty motors and stiffer frames. For occasional running, a well-specified ProForm with a full-length deck and adequate continuous horsepower is usually fine. Check deck length and CHP on the exact model.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is the NordicTrack warranty better than ProForm?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Not reliably. At comparable price points the terms are often similar on paper, and they change between model years. Read the warranty for each exact model, comparing motor, parts and labour separately rather than the headline frame figure, and check whether in-home service is included.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

